</boilerplate><preface><clause type="toc" id="_13d7055e-30fc-845a-c60e-8972faf092d9" displayorder="1"><fmt-title depth="1" id="_b7371af6-75a1-52fa-2891-5c5f9a06aa7c">Contents</fmt-title></clause>
<abstract id="_c3f98905-4287-b3b0-7610-de952ec586c9" semx-id="_c3f98905-4287-b3b0-7610-de952ec586c9" displayorder="2"><title id="_c51f08e5-f95a-09ed-e867-10be652f8308" semx-id="_37c298bf-5619-a5c6-817b-d777b5ead0b1">Abstract</title><fmt-title depth="1" id="_749ba5c6-ce5f-3642-db11-4613c40c12f3"><span class="fmt-caption-label">I<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_c51f08e5-f95a-09ed-e867-10be652f8308">Abstract</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><semx element="title" source="_c3f98905-4287-b3b0-7610-de952ec586c9">Abstract</semx></fmt-xref-label><p id="_b4d631e4-50d8-2119-ed67-c3d84456c532" semx-id="_b4d631e4-50d8-2119-ed67-c3d84456c532">This Standard defines the open CityGML Conceptual Model for the storage and exchange of virtual 3D city models. The CityGML Conceptual Model is defined by a Unified Modeling Language (UML) object model. This UML model builds on the ISO Technical Committee 211 (ISO/TC 211) conceptual model standards for spatial and temporal data. Building on the ISO foundation assures that the man-made features described in the city models share the same spatiotemporal universe as the surrounding countryside within which they reside.</p>

<p id="_59498cf6-8047-d07b-3e41-b11c65cbc731" semx-id="_59498cf6-8047-d07b-3e41-b11c65cbc731">A key goal for the development of the CityGML Conceptual Model is to provide a common definition of the basic entities, attributes, and relations of a 3D city model. This is especially important with respect to the cost-effective sustainable maintenance of 3D city models, allowing the reuse of the same data in different application fields.</p>

<p id="_2eb6e50e-6d29-2982-d30c-f5e1e7548edb" semx-id="_2eb6e50e-6d29-2982-d30c-f5e1e7548edb">The class models described in this standard are also available at <link target="https://github.com/opengeospatial/CityGML3-Workspace/tree/1.0/UML/CityGML" id="_1025be91-2350-7647-4979-147f45869333"/><fmt-link target="https://github.com/opengeospatial/CityGML3-Workspace/tree/1.0/UML/CityGML"/></p>
</abstract><clause id="_e2afbf4a-c1ac-4c06-23b0-87a8d073345c" type="keywords" displayorder="3">
<title id="_2aa64cc4-77bd-7a2b-1a90-7fae2dc8001f">Keywords</title><fmt-title depth="1" id="_febab828-4cd5-e6a3-a222-ac3f671a4e90"><span class="fmt-caption-label">II<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_2aa64cc4-77bd-7a2b-1a90-7fae2dc8001f">Keywords</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><semx element="title" source="_e2afbf4a-c1ac-4c06-23b0-87a8d073345c">Keywords</semx></fmt-xref-label>
<p>The following are keywords to be used by search engines and document catalogues.</p>
<p>ogcdoc, OGC document, CityGML, 3D city models</p></clause>
<clause type="security" id="_089bc373-1e6c-a75e-d8b1-b1720c114978" obligation="informative" semx-id="_089bc373-1e6c-a75e-d8b1-b1720c114978" displayorder="4">
