</clause>
</clause>

<clause id="section-EAPK_E1321C0B_B95B_44c0_A3EA_3B507911CD78" anchor="section-EAPK_E1321C0B_B95B_44c0_A3EA_3B507911CD78" obligation="normative" semx-id="_229a078c-2971-bac1-11b8-9e03c6615ba0">
<title id="_c69071ab-71ec-2c75-72d7-ffa6f5260815" semx-id="_29a99f72-b9a3-4a27-4659-055e9d06b430">CityFurniture</title><fmt-title depth="2" id="_d18b016c-d0d2-0b39-c8ba-f389f5cabd4c"><span class="fmt-caption-label">7<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>4<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span><semx element="title" source="_c69071ab-71ec-2c75-72d7-ffa6f5260815">CityFurniture</semx></fmt-title><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Clause</span> 7<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>4</fmt-xref-label>
<requirement id="_07283efb-97cd-4e27-947f-456ddca38656" anchor="rc_cityfurniture" model="ogc" type="class" semx-id="_e9daf721-324e-e07c-ba96-04a02d21ae43" autonum="3" original-id="rc_cityfurniture"><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Requirements class</span> 3</fmt-xref-label><inherit id="_3039ba1a-acdc-4dc3-88cc-67ad61e7a757"><xref target="rc_core">/req/req-class-core</xref></inherit> <subject id="_7bca0cc1-a3bf-4649-a05e-5c406da55113">Implementation Specification</subject>

<fmt-provision id="_4ca917f9-5e94-9863-048a-fdab6943dc9d"><table id="rc_cityfurniture" type="recommendclass" class="modspec"><thead><tr><th scope="colgroup" colspan="2"><p class="RecommendationTitle"><fmt-name id="_8febd85d-d5e7-58a1-36c8-bb6b6d2b8d26"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">Requirements class</span> 3</span></fmt-name></p></th></tr></thead>
<tbody><tr><th>Target type</th><td><semx element="subject" source="_7bca0cc1-a3bf-4649-a05e-5c406da55113">Implementation Specification</semx></td></tr><tr><th>Prerequisite</th><td><semx element="inherit" source="_3039ba1a-acdc-4dc3-88cc-67ad61e7a757"><xref target="rc_core" id="_40b8dcc1-9c85-b9d6-b354-a45fe8e23087">/req/req-class-core</xref><fmt-xref target="rc_core">/req/req-class-core</fmt-xref></semx></td></tr></tbody></table></fmt-provision></requirement>

<p id="_e77dac14-290c-c020-5f01-963e514adbde" semx-id="_e77dac14-290c-c020-5f01-963e514adbde">The CityFurniture module provides the representation of objects or pieces of equipment that are installed in the outdoor environment for various purposes, such as decoration, explanation, or control. City furniture objects are relatively small, immovable objects and usually are of prototypical or geotypical form. Examples include road signs, traffic signals, bicycle racks, street lamps, fountains, flower buckets, advertising columns, and benches.</p>

<p id="_65a251e7-e414-9b95-1f29-1011d4366435" semx-id="_65a251e7-e414-9b95-1f29-1011d4366435">City furniture is represented in the UML model by the top-level feature type <em>CityFurniture</em>, which is also the only class of the CityFurniture module.</p>

<p id="_8f7d124a-6bd1-d95f-623e-eb4066c8f125" semx-id="_8f7d124a-6bd1-d95f-623e-eb4066c8f125">The UML diagram of the CityFurniture module is depicted in <xref target="cityfurniture-uml" id="_4e91ee65-94ef-4e0c-0abb-d6691492a9af"/><fmt-xref target="cityfurniture-uml"><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 29</fmt-xref>. A detailed discussion of this Requirements Class can be found in the <link target="http://docs.opengeospatial.org/DRAFTS/20-066.html#ug-model-city-furniture-section" id="_c9761bc0-7afa-02e0-cb02-d89a6b21b5ba">CityGML 3.0 Users Guide</link><fmt-link target="http://docs.opengeospatial.org/DRAFTS/20-066.html#ug-model-city-furniture-section">CityGML 3.0 Users Guide</fmt-link>.</p>

<figure id="cityfurniture-uml" anchor="cityfurniture-uml" semx-id="_3790b4f9-dacb-3f23-c7f8-8c3e5fdb41e7" autonum="29">
<name id="_1a57488a-b98b-3473-72eb-347e45689d68" semx-id="_ac59e6ba-3e8f-9ec5-6a57-8536c49cd6d1">UML diagram of CityGML’s City Furniture model.</name><fmt-name id="_8786ae60-c561-6116-8c75-12fd93e0656d"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 29</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"> — </span><semx element="name" source="_1a57488a-b98b-3473-72eb-347e45689d68">UML diagram of CityGML’s City Furniture model.</semx></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 29</fmt-xref-label>
<image id="_e43d948c-997a-8bdf-2733-9acd90135e91" src="/__w/ogc-citygml-xmi/ogc-citygml-xmi/_site/documents/standard/_tmp_images_77d3242a-680f-4d67-85ca-3c09a9100559/8157be07-e0a1-49c0-8f3f-b0c1d5dfcd18.png" extracted="true" mimetype="image/png" height="auto" width="auto" filename="figures/CityFurniture.png" semx-id="_e43d948c-997a-8bdf-2733-9acd90135e91"/></figure>

<p id="_e5ca887f-20f5-fa9a-3a04-878e4efa98fd" semx-id="_e5ca887f-20f5-fa9a-3a04-878e4efa98fd">The ADE data types and Code Lists provided for the CityFurniture module are illustrated in <xref target="cityfurniture-uml-ade-types" id="_de8b5e2c-734c-6fa2-3fc0-7fa3f74c5ca0"/><fmt-xref target="cityfurniture-uml-ade-types"><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 30</fmt-xref>.</p>

<figure id="cityfurniture-uml-ade-types" anchor="cityfurniture-uml-ade-types" semx-id="_655908ac-edf9-1928-0247-174ad2061e18" autonum="30">
<name id="_763f8e83-d712-3d40-3736-7897b624f2eb" semx-id="_78ed3c91-b778-7c4d-d31b-7429c36e8788">ADE classes and Code Lists of the CityGML CityFurniture module.</name><fmt-name id="_73eafabc-36b5-f1bf-9b2d-48bebdc037e2"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 30</span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"> — </span><semx element="name" source="_763f8e83-d712-3d40-3736-7897b624f2eb">ADE classes and Code Lists of the CityGML CityFurniture module.</semx></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Figure</span> 30</fmt-xref-label>
<image id="_480eef0c-b665-d33c-93c3-ecd62b14a091" src="/__w/ogc-citygml-xmi/ogc-citygml-xmi/_site/documents/standard/_tmp_images_77d3242a-680f-4d67-85ca-3c09a9100559/2864fb34-da78-4709-aac1-a4715f439532.png" extracted="true" mimetype="image/png" height="auto" width="auto" filename="figures/CityFurniture-with_codelists_and_ADE_datatypes.png" semx-id="_480eef0c-b665-d33c-93c3-ecd62b14a091"/></figure>

<p id="_c039077f-c0fe-bf17-2fa9-9cb99d5450ed" semx-id="_c039077f-c0fe-bf17-2fa9-9cb99d5450ed"><xref target="cityfurniture-boundaries-table" id="_97365e0c-e1d0-b0ad-ed35-3c0ab07d11e8"/><fmt-xref target="cityfurniture-boundaries-table"><span class="fmt-element-name">Table</span> 17</fmt-xref> lists the surfaces that are allowed as thematic surface boundaries of the space classes defined in the CityFurniture module:</p>

