<note id="_3943a6c5-9284-85ff-6644-95e7e386049f" semx-id="_3943a6c5-9284-85ff-6644-95e7e386049f" autonum=""><fmt-name id="_09bb1474-1546-90a9-4795-97a623ce04f4"><span class="fmt-caption-label"><span class="fmt-element-name">NOTE</span></span><span class="fmt-label-delim">:<tab/></span></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Note</span></fmt-xref-label><fmt-xref-label container="_6313dfce-ed06-4c80-c524-d8bf17b4a93d"><span class="fmt-xref-container"><span class="fmt-element-name">Table</span> 90</span><span class="fmt-comma">,</span> <span class="fmt-element-name">Note</span></fmt-xref-label><p id="_e7998d83-4238-4796-2c28-2b4b271324ad" semx-id="_e7998d83-4238-4796-2c28-2b4b271324ad">In most cases, the state of a GM_Point is fully determined by its position attribute. The only exception to this is if the GM_Point has been subclassed to provide additional non-geometric information such as symbology.</p>
</note>
