<tbody><tr id="_07fa184c-e70e-f3c9-a50c-3ecfda4c4cbe" semx-id="_07fa184c-e70e-f3c9-a50c-3ecfda4c4cbe"><th id="_e7449629-fc4f-c890-f257-97b783546920" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_e7449629-fc4f-c890-f257-97b783546920">Definition:</th>
<td id="_b09fbcf5-ca9f-2ef7-54ac-be22f0b86a8d" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_b09fbcf5-ca9f-2ef7-54ac-be22f0b86a8d"><p id="_947ed4fb-957b-72fc-51fe-91a9aa2e7ed4" semx-id="_947ed4fb-957b-72fc-51fe-91a9aa2e7ed4">AbstractSpaceBoundary is the abstract superclass for all types of space boundaries. A space boundary is an entity with areal extent in the real world. Space boundaries are objects that bound a Space. They also realize the contact between adjacent spaces.</p>
</td>
</tr><tr id="_bbf230fb-ea98-adef-dcdc-3636bfe6738b" semx-id="_bbf230fb-ea98-adef-dcdc-3636bfe6738b"><th id="_79370891-a1d4-2db6-cdef-a6141ebd2ff7" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_79370891-a1d4-2db6-cdef-a6141ebd2ff7">Subclass of:</th>
