<tbody><tr id="_cda782e4-cd56-8b8b-3ef4-13a35f67204f" semx-id="_cda782e4-cd56-8b8b-3ef4-13a35f67204f"><th id="_e4603718-fb8f-f8b9-2c7e-bb34b95abfe7" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_e4603718-fb8f-f8b9-2c7e-bb34b95abfe7">Definition:</th>
<td id="_ae474a9c-08b6-c7a8-5597-3fb1c647a4e8" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_ae474a9c-08b6-c7a8-5597-3fb1c647a4e8"><p id="_89fb7b5f-1663-8e8c-750d-6f764a4d0ea6" semx-id="_89fb7b5f-1663-8e8c-750d-6f764a4d0ea6">ImplicitGeometry is a geometry representation where the shape is stored only once as a prototypical geometry. Examples are a tree or other vegetation object, a traffic light or a traffic sign. This prototypic geometry object can be re-used or referenced many times, wherever the corresponding feature occurs in the 3D city model.</p>
</td>
</tr><tr id="_9773a537-2d5c-4261-e40b-cf5d65a326c5" semx-id="_9773a537-2d5c-4261-e40b-cf5d65a326c5"><th id="_34fee90f-e48c-f1b1-7ae3-8f737eeeb9e9" valign="middle" align="left" semx-id="_34fee90f-e48c-f1b1-7ae3-8f737eeeb9e9">Subclass of:</th>
