<p id="_36b4a677-ce4a-d140-be26-d5fb4ffb3337" semx-id="_36b4a677-ce4a-d140-be26-d5fb4ffb3337">The following concepts from the ISO TC211 Harmonized UML model are referenced by the CityGML Conceptual UML model but do not play a major role in its’ definition. They are provided here to support a more complete understanding of the model.</p>

<term id="term-Area" anchor="term-Area" semx-id="_7361c4cd-3c09-2197-501d-618f1f56a932" autonum="B.1.2.1"><fmt-name id="_ebd27572-7607-ee04-37a2-6cf5359ff909"><span class="fmt-caption-label">B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>1<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>2<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>1<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span></span></fmt-name><fmt-xref-label><span class="fmt-element-name">Annex</span> B<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>1<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>2<span class="fmt-autonum-delim">.</span>1</fmt-xref-label><preferred id="_0ecc4bc3-87d2-c828-0bf6-6f4874f7a5be"><expression>
<name id="_5c6ebbbf-f1dd-7740-260c-c62135d234e1">Area</name>
</expression>
</preferred><fmt-preferred><p><semx element="preferred" source="_0ecc4bc3-87d2-c828-0bf6-6f4874f7a5be"><strong><semx element="expression/name" source="_5c6ebbbf-f1dd-7740-260c-c62135d234e1">Area</semx></strong></semx></p></fmt-preferred>
<definition id="_e995a79a-9e00-742f-b9fc-484080493763" semx-id="_e995a79a-9e00-742f-b9fc-484080493763"><verbal-definition semx-id="_b02239c4-ceeb-e02f-4b7f-ce97baa1b235" id="_b02239c4-ceeb-e02f-4b7f-ce97baa1b235"><p semx-id="_40ea5054-819a-18be-0952-dc3ccb5a4bb6" original-id="_40ea5054-819a-18be-0952-dc3ccb5a4bb6">The measure of the physical extent of any topologically 2-D geometric object. Usually measured in “square” units of length.</p></verbal-definition></definition><fmt-definition id="_c34050dd-cbc6-c1d6-6955-25aba8c4ea2b"><semx element="definition" source="_e995a79a-9e00-742f-b9fc-484080493763"><p id="_40ea5054-819a-18be-0952-dc3ccb5a4bb6" semx-id="_40ea5054-819a-18be-0952-dc3ccb5a4bb6">The measure of the physical extent of any topologically 2-D geometric object. Usually measured in “square” units of length.</p></semx></fmt-definition>


 <source status="identical" type="authoritative" id="_abd9b53a-d9cc-ef97-5da1-7953a5ba359c"><origin bibitemid="iso19103" type="inline" citeas="ISO 19103:2015"/></source><fmt-termsource status="identical" type="authoritative">[<strong>SOURCE:</strong> <semx element="source" source="_abd9b53a-d9cc-ef97-5da1-7953a5ba359c"><origin bibitemid="iso19103" type="inline" citeas="ISO 19103:2015" id="_a2b529c8-ef1b-4fac-ccc1-4eaedcec8b6f"/><semx element="origin" source="_a2b529c8-ef1b-4fac-ccc1-4eaedcec8b6f"><fmt-xref type="inline" target="iso19103">ISO 19103:2015</fmt-xref></semx></semx>]</fmt-termsource></term>

