<definition id="_41faa2de-1b7a-2c02-ea14-d38b808ce8c2" semx-id="_41faa2de-1b7a-2c02-ea14-d38b808ce8c2"><verbal-definition semx-id="_4b7aea2d-193a-fc43-66d3-d4f300eab720" id="_4b7aea2d-193a-fc43-66d3-d4f300eab720"><p semx-id="_a8115634-dad5-2b09-c6ae-0de64f0cfd5e" original-id="_a8115634-dad5-2b09-c6ae-0de64f0cfd5e">GM_Surface and GM_SurfacePatch both represent sections of surface geometry, and therefore share a number of operation signatures. These are defined in the interface class GM_GenericSurface.</p></verbal-definition></definition><fmt-definition id="_9e1acbd5-4e59-e426-fd9f-7afb463b32a3"><semx element="definition" source="_41faa2de-1b7a-2c02-ea14-d38b808ce8c2"><p id="_a8115634-dad5-2b09-c6ae-0de64f0cfd5e" semx-id="_a8115634-dad5-2b09-c6ae-0de64f0cfd5e">GM_Surface and GM_SurfacePatch both represent sections of surface geometry, and therefore share a number of operation signatures. These are defined in the interface class GM_GenericSurface.</p></semx></fmt-definition>


